From c2378e10b7b7f4b5802bb9f71bc51cde0edb8168 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayoub5550 <140963656+ayoub5550@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 02:52:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(arm64): step 0 -- SharpEmu as a native
 linux-bionic-arm64 process, null CPU backend

Publishes with NativeAOT for linux-bionic-arm64 (NDK clang as the linker,
PublishAotUsingRuntimePack) and runs everything up to the first guest instruction
natively, with no x86-64 translator underneath:
- HostPlatform: the POSIX platform on linux-arm64 (memory, threads, audio, input are
  plain POSIX; the emitted-stub resolver is only reached from the x64 backend)
- CpuDispatcher: refuses guest execution in a non-x64 process before any x86-64 stub
  is emitted (the null backend)
- CLI: warns instead of exiting on linux-arm64
- lean warm-up: leaves the crypto/net-security framework initializers to first use on
  a non-x64 host -- on Android they load the OpenSSL shim, which finds BoringSSL,
  misses a2d_ASN1_OBJECT and aborts the process
- SHARPEMU_BENCH=shader[:iterations[:instructions]]: an in-process timing of the
  emulator's own CPU work (decode + SPIR-V translation of a synthetic Gen5 shader),
  to compare a build under a translator with a native one
